WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.634
-A bizarre, and, ultimately,

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:03.901
pointless, drama

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.901
unfolded yesterday
after Piers Morgan,

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:08.300
an on-and-off friend and ally
of Donald Trump,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.267
debuted a trailer
for an interview

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.968
in which he claimed
Trump angrily walked out

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.400
and then Trump
later released audio

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.167
he claimed contradicted
the trailer

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:20.133
and showed that, in reality,
the ending was cordial.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.100
Also, coup plotter Rudy Giuliani
was on "The Masked Singer."

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.100
[ Laughter ]
For more on this --

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.868
Wait, do we want more on this?

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:27.801
Alright, we do?
Alright.

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.567
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.300
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.234
♪♪
[ Whistling ]

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:39.100
Republican politics, these days,
is often so relentlessly stupid,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.534
it generally feels like we're
being punished for something.

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:44.534
[ Laughter ]
It's like we got busted
watching an episode of "Maury"

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.667
and God said,
"Okay, you like that?

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.734
How about if everything is
an episode of 'Maury'

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.133
[ Laughter ]
from now on?

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.734
Do you like that?"

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:53.734
Every damn day, we have to deal
with something insane,

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:55.701
like stories
about congressional orgies

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.934
or senators writing
Disney erotica

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:00.834
or cable hosts
pitching testicle tanning,

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:01.868
[ Laughter ]
and it always seems to come

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.300
from the same cluster
of weirdos,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.801
like Ted Cruz, Tucker Carlson,
Rudy Giuliani, Donald Trump,

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.968
Matt Gaetz, Madison Cawthorn,
and Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:10.267
[ Laughter ]
Their names are all starting
to blend together now

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.000
in one soup of insanity.
Did you hear

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.834
what Muckerie Gaelor Cawthump
said now?

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:15.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.000
Did someone flip a switch
or something

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.667
that unleashed
all these weirdos on us?

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.400
It's like that scene
in "Ghostbusters"

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.901
where the EPA guy
makes them open the vault

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.467
and all the ghosts
come flying out.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.868
[ Laughter ]
I mean, I could've sworn

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:27.534
I saw the zombie cabdriver

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.300
on "The Masked Singer"
last night.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.100
Yeah.
You saw that Rudy Giuliani,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.367
the guy who waged a lengthy
and unhinged campaign

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:36.767
to overturn the 2020 election,

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:39.033
who tried to help Donald Trump
steal millions of votes,

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.968
helped orchestrate a scheme
to extort the country of Ukraine

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.501
to help Trump cheat
in the election,

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:46.067
had his home and office
raided by the FBI,

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.634
is currently
under federal investigation

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:48.667
for various allegations,

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.601
and called for a trial
by combat

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:53.234
on the day of the
January 6th insurrection,

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.634
was on Fox's "Masked Singer"
last night.

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:59.467
That's a terrible, terrible
thing to do to people on 4/20.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:00.667
[ Stoner voice ]
Hey, man.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.701
[ Laughter, ohs, and applause ]

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.367
Hey, man,
that weed you gave me,

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:06.200
I think it's laced
with something, man.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:09.801
I'm seeing some
[bleep]-up [bleep], man!

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:14.734
And, when he was unmasked,
everyone was shocked,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.501
including, apparently,
Rudy himself.

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:17.968
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.334
-Oh, my goodness!

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:22.634
Former associate
attorney general,

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:25.033
former mayor of New York City.

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.267
-Is that Robert Duval?

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:28.267
-No, that's not Robert Duval.

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:31.133
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Rudy Giuliani!

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.734
-No! way!

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.267
-Oh...my...
-Oh, my God!

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:37.634
[ Fireworks explode ]
-gosh.

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:40.300
[ Laughter ]
-Well, Mr. Giuliani,

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.367
with all of the controversy

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.667
that's surrounding you
right now,

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.400
I think it surprises us all
that you're here

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.200
on "The Masked Singer."

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.634
-Me too!

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:51.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.167
-I'm sure he was surprised.

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.133
There's a good chance
Rudy genuinely

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.334
did not know where he was

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.234
[ Laughter and applause ]
and was just as surprised

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.067
as everyone else
when they opened that box.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.734
He was probably thrilled,
by the way.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:02.834
[ As Giuliani ]
A singing competition?

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.634
I just assumed
I was going to jail.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:05.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.300
I bet you could trick
Rudy Giuliani

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.601
into climbing
into almost any container,

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.200
just by telling him
there's a trove

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.634
of shredded Trump ballots
in there or, I don't know,

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.534
a bottle of scotch
that wasn't completely empty.

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:18.501
[ Laughter ]
Honestly, the idea
that any TV show

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:21.634
would help rehabilitate a key
figure in an attempted coup

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.567
for entertainment purposes is
so disgusting and shocking.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.634
The only reality show
I would've been okay

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.300
with Rudy being on is
"Love Is Blind"...

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.434
just to see if he accidentally

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:32.968
ends up marrying
his cousin again.

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:35.234
[ Static crackling ]
So, where are you from?

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:37.000
32 East Flatbush Road?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.367
That's where my aunt
and uncle live!

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:39.868
We got so much in common.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.734
And I'm sorry.
Whenever we make that joke,

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.033
I'm supposed to clarify
that it was

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.734
his second cousin
he married, you know,

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:48.267
as in someone who you share
a great-grandparent with,

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:51.133
not the second time
he married his cousin.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.400
[ Laughter ]
Although I could definitely

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.501
see Rudy doing that twice
by accident, too.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.334
[ As Giuliani ]
Honey, I was just looking
at the marriage certificate.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:04:00.367
You accidentally put Giuliani
on the line for maiden name.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.067
Giuliani is your maiden name?!

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:03.901
Oh, Rudy, you done it again!

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:06.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:07.901
And, again, I should clarify,
you know,

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:10.133
all jokes aside here,

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.467
when he married
his second cousin,

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:12.767
which is a real thing he did,

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.534
her maiden name wasn't Giuliani.

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.267
I mean, this man was the mayor
of New York City.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:18.367
How dare I treat him
like some sort of clown?

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.834
[ Laughter ]
Oh, well, alright.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.267
I guess it's fair now.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:23.701
[ Laughter ]
You know who probably panicked

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:26.234
when Rudy Giuliani appeared
as a Jack-in-the-Box?

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.033
This guy.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.167
[ Laughter ]
"Yeah.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.000
I'm going to lay low
for a while."

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.100
[ Laughter ]
And yet, somehow, that was not

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.868
the only incredibly stupid
thing to happen

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:36.033
in Republican politics yesterday
because one of Trump's

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:38.601
longtime friends and allies,
Piers Morgan,

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.968
released an overly
dramatic trailer

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:42.400
for a new interview with Trump,

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.801
where he claimed Trump angrily
stormed out of the interview

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.801
when pressed
about his election lies.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:48.901
-Okay, Piers, I'm ready.

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.534
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:52.701
-I'll be completely straight
to your face.

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.267
-I think I'm a very honest man.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:55.734
Much more honest
than you, actually.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:56.734
-Really?!
-Yeah.

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:58.067
-It was a free
and fair election.

00:04:58.067 --> 00:04:59.934
You lost.
-Only a fool would think that.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.501
-You think I'm a fool?
-I do now, yeah.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.567
-With respect --
-Excuse me.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.033
-With respect,
you haven't produced

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.267
the hard evidence.
-Excuse me.

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:08.467
I don't think you're real.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.100
[ Voices overlapping ]
Very dishonest.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.167
Let's finish up the interview.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:13.234
Turn the camera off.

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:13.901
♪♪

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:15.033
Very dishonest.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.801
-I'm sorry,
but who edited that trailer,

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:17.767
Michael Bay?

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:20.901
Was there hand-to-hand combat?

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.067
Is this from the next
Jason Bourne movie,

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:25.200
where, instead of advanced
fighting skills,

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.200
Jason Bourne wakes up
in a poorly tailored suit?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.300
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.567
By the way, Piers Morgan himself

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:32.501
also famously
stormed off the set

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:34.200
of his own TV show in the UK

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.767
when he was challenged
on something he said.

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:38.200
These guys constantly call
the left snowflakes

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.234
and "get triggered,"
and then they

00:05:40.234 --> 00:05:41.868
immediately melt down
when confronted

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:44.634
by even the gentlest questioning
from a friendly source.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:45.734
I mean, look at Trump's face.

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:47.200
He's literally melting down.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:50.000
That's what a Yankee candle
looks like,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.234
if you leave it out in the sun.

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:52.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:55.033
I believe that one is called...

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:57.234
[ Laughter, ohs, and applause ]
It will never not shock me

00:05:57.234 --> 00:06:02.534
that anyone in the country
looks at that guy and says,

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:03.567
"That's a face I can trust."

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:06.868
That looks like a mask
you'd rip off

00:06:06.868 --> 00:06:09.367
to reveal Rudy Giuliani
on "The Masked Singer."

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:11.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
But then a weird thing happened,

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:13.901
where Trump's team
released audio

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:16.367
claiming he didn't
angrily walk out.

00:06:16.367 --> 00:06:17.300
NBC News reported that...

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:35.634
Genuine fights don't end

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:37.400
with "Thank you very much.
I really appreciate it."

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.234
You've never seen
a ten-minute fight sequence

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:40.868
in a movie with The Rock
and Vin Diesel

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:42.334
punching each other
on top of a train,

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:44.400
dodging bullets, laying flat
when they go through a tunnel,

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.934
popping up again,
doing a windmill kick

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:48.267
to the other guy's face that
sends him flying off the train,

00:06:48.267 --> 00:06:50.467
leading the other guy to relax
and assume the fight's over,

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:52.701
only to realize it's not over
because his nemesis climbs back

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:55.033
up onto the train after having
clung to a door handle...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:56.334
...so they fight
for another 10 minutes,

00:06:56.334 --> 00:06:58.267
until both of them wrestle
each other back and forth

00:06:58.267 --> 00:06:59.767
and fall dramatically
off the train,

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:01.901
across the river,
and continue to punch in midair

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:03.901
as they plunge 100 feet
into the icy rapids,

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:05.334
tumbling towards a waterfall,

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:07.601
where they cling to a rock,
until they lose their grip,

00:07:07.601 --> 00:07:08.767
and then they grab
onto a tree branch,

00:07:08.767 --> 00:07:09.901
narrowly escaping death,

00:07:09.901 --> 00:07:11.367
and then they turn
to each other and say,

00:07:11.367 --> 00:07:12.501
"Hey, man,
that was a great fight.

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:13.701
Thanks so much."

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:15.968
[ Laughter and applause ]
Of course -- Of course...

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.934
[ Cheering ]

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:20.100
...if it was Vin Diesel,

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.334
he wouldn't say that.
He would say --

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:22.534
[ As Diesel ]
It's all about family.

00:07:22.534 --> 00:07:25.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:28.267 --> 00:07:30.434
That's today's
in-Vin-cible impression.

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:31.501
[ Engine vrooms ]

00:07:31.501 --> 00:07:35.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.601
That's what he said
when he pitched it.

00:07:36.601 --> 00:07:37.434
[ As Diesel ]
It's all about family.

00:07:37.434 --> 00:07:38.901
They're like, "But also cars?"

00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:42.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.667 --> 00:07:43.534
What are we talking about?

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:44.868
Oh, right.

00:07:44.868 --> 00:07:46.434
And Trump's account
would make sense

00:07:46.434 --> 00:07:49.667
because even the initial
description of the interview

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:51.000
had this odd anecdote --

00:07:59.434 --> 00:08:00.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:08.367
It's so funny
you can trick Trump

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.901
into sitting for an interview
if you just ask him about golf.

00:08:10.901 --> 00:08:12.934
He's so easy to checkmate.
It's like how you

00:08:12.934 --> 00:08:14.334
[ Laughter ]
trick a golden retriever

00:08:14.334 --> 00:08:17.033
into running after a tennis ball
by pretending to throw it.

00:08:17.033 --> 00:08:19.434
[ Laughter ]
In Trump's case,
he'd just spend hours walking

00:08:19.434 --> 00:08:21.501
around the White House lawn,
looking for it.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.267
[ As Trump ]
Where's this freaking
tennis ball?

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:24.634
I ran all the way here.

00:08:24.634 --> 00:08:25.801
I ran to find the tenni--

00:08:25.801 --> 00:08:27.167
If I don't get that tennis ball,

00:08:27.167 --> 00:08:28.834
I'm not going to get that treat
and, let me tell you,

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:30.133
I want that Milk-Bone.

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:32.601
[ Laughter ]
We love Milk-Bone,
don't we, folks?

00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.734 --> 00:08:37.434
It combines the flavor of milk
with beef, chicken.

00:08:37.434 --> 00:08:40.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:43.467
What we're seeing here is that,
to all these guys,

00:08:43.467 --> 00:08:46.033
whether it's Piers Morgan
or "The Masked Singer,"

00:08:46.033 --> 00:08:47.434
it's all just entertainment.

00:08:47.434 --> 00:08:49.901
They don't care
about what's actually at stake,

00:08:49.901 --> 00:08:51.400
which is our democracy,
and, deep down,

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.267
most Republicans know it.
They know the truth.

00:08:53.267 --> 00:08:54.934
As we learned from a bombshell

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:56.234
New York Times report
this morning

00:08:56.234 --> 00:08:58.133
that revealed
senior GOP leaders,

00:08:58.133 --> 00:08:59.601
including Kevin McCarthy
and Mitch McConnell,

00:08:59.601 --> 00:09:02.067
were ready to push Trump
out of office

00:09:02.067 --> 00:09:03.968
in the days after the
January 6th insurrection,

00:09:03.968 --> 00:09:05.734
before changing their tune
and deciding

00:09:05.734 --> 00:09:08.400
to stick with him
for political expediency.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.434
-This morning, we're learning
that the nation's

00:09:10.434 --> 00:09:12.601
top two Republicans
had serious concerns

00:09:12.601 --> 00:09:15.067
about former President Trump's
ability to lead

00:09:15.067 --> 00:09:18.467
in the wake of the January 6th
attack on the U.S. Capitol.

00:09:18.467 --> 00:09:19.701
The New York Times is reporting

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:21.801
that House Minority Leader
Kevin McCarthy

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:23.167
told other Republican leaders

00:09:23.167 --> 00:09:26.634
that he was going to advise
President Trump to resign.

00:09:26.634 --> 00:09:28.367
The Times is also reporting
that McCarthy

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.767
and Senate Minority Leader
Mitch McConnell looked

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.968
into the 25th Amendment
as an option

00:09:32.968 --> 00:09:34.801
for removing Trump from office.

00:09:34.801 --> 00:09:37.267
-McCarthy, specifically,
the reporting says

00:09:37.267 --> 00:09:40.467
he wanted to push Trump
to resign,

00:09:40.467 --> 00:09:43.033
that he said,
"I've had it with this guy."

00:09:43.033 --> 00:09:44.167
-I feel like, in the wake

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:45.901
of a violent attack
on the Capitol,

00:09:45.901 --> 00:09:48.000
you should be able to muster
something a little stronger

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.934
than "I've had it
with that guy."

00:09:49.934 --> 00:09:51.901
[ Laughter ]
Even their strongest
denunciations of Trump

00:09:51.901 --> 00:09:54.701
behind closed doors sounds like
your dad complaining to you

00:09:54.701 --> 00:09:56.501
about the guy
who does his landscaping.

00:09:56.501 --> 00:09:57.400
"I've had it with this guy.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:58.701
He keeps using the wrong mulch

00:09:58.701 --> 00:09:59.901
and all my petunias are dying.

00:09:59.901 --> 00:10:01.467
Alright, here's your mom."

00:10:01.467 --> 00:10:03.968
[ Laughter ]
But this has always
been the case.

00:10:03.968 --> 00:10:05.300
Behind the scenes,
they all knew --

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.634
every single one of them --
how dangerous Trump was.

00:10:07.634 --> 00:10:09.434
But they need him for the
show business of it all.

00:10:09.434 --> 00:10:12.033
Trump's like their
unmanageable Broadway diva.

00:10:12.033 --> 00:10:14.434
"Shirley stabbed the wardrobe
guy with a chopstick

00:10:14.434 --> 00:10:15.467
and he's threatening to sue.

00:10:15.467 --> 00:10:17.033
Plus, she's drunk as a skunk

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:18.267
and curtain's in 10 minutes,

00:10:18.267 --> 00:10:20.000
but goddamn it,
that broad can sing."

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.133 --> 00:10:23.300
A good rule of thumb
with these guys is,

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.734
whenever you can't tell
if they're dumb or evil,

00:10:25.734 --> 00:10:26.868
the answer is all of the above.

00:10:26.868 --> 00:10:28.133
[ Laughter ]
Republicans calculated they

00:10:28.133 --> 00:10:30.434
could use Trump
for sinister political purposes

00:10:30.434 --> 00:10:31.701
and, once again,
that's what happened

00:10:31.701 --> 00:10:33.601
because,
as The New York Times reports...

00:10:40.434 --> 00:10:42.467
And McCarthy even flew
down to Mar-a-Lago

00:10:42.467 --> 00:10:44.868
to kiss Trump's ring
and pose for that photo

00:10:44.868 --> 00:10:47.501
where they look like
two personal injury attorneys

00:10:47.501 --> 00:10:51.000
who want to know if you have
asbestos in your house.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.701
"Do you have asbestos?
Well, so do we.

00:10:52.701 --> 00:10:54.400
In fact,
we accidentally ate some.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.167
Wait.
What was this commercial about?

00:10:56.167 --> 00:10:57.934
I don't know.
My memory's not so good

00:10:57.934 --> 00:10:59.734
since I ate that asbestos.

00:10:59.734 --> 00:11:01.934
So call us and tell us
what our names are.

00:11:01.934 --> 00:11:02.934
We can't remember!"

00:11:02.934 --> 00:11:04.300
[ Laughter ]

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.334
The fate of our democracy is
very much on the brink

00:11:06.334 --> 00:11:07.901
and yet, so many
of our institutions,

00:11:07.901 --> 00:11:09.968
from political parties
to media organizations,

00:11:09.968 --> 00:11:11.767
are far too willing
to rehabilitate

00:11:11.767 --> 00:11:13.701
the key perpetrators
of a slow-moving coup,

00:11:13.701 --> 00:11:17.100
all for entertainment
or profit or political gain.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:19.367
The rot in our political system
goes deep.

00:11:19.367 --> 00:11:20.167
These guys are all...

00:11:20.167 --> 00:11:21.767
-♪ Bad to the bone ♪

00:11:21.767 --> 00:11:24.701
[ Laughter ]

00:11:27.767 --> 00:11:30.067
Is our wah-wah horn broken?

00:11:30.067 --> 00:11:31.601
[ Laughter ]

00:11:31.601 --> 00:11:33.534
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:33.534 --> 00:11:37.033
♪♪

